    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We have 300 proteins and 150 metabolites measured in plasma from the same 60 marathon runners, with matching sample IDs. To pick candidate mechanisms, I want one overall map of which proteins and metabolites are directly linked to each other once all the other measured molecules are taken into account."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want one overall map of which proteins and metabolites are directly linked to each other once all the other measured molecules are taken into account.\" -- available from DRAGON.\n\n**DRAGON**. DRAGON fits a two-layer Gaussian graphical model with layer-aware shrinkage. Partial correlations describe associations conditional on the other measured features under that model; they are not directed causal effects. The two omics layers must refer to matched samples.\n\nYou would need DRAGON omics layer 1, DRAGON omics layer 2. The analysis would provide inferred associations between omics features.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
